  "body": "## Current-source continuation, not a restart\n\nThis follows the complete new source-control chapter **ISM1\u201343** at main **`331ccd30185a98bfc8fde8102cf09b9c2add4d6b`**, especially its signed finite-resolvent construction (ISM27\u201337) and proper-source kernel (ISM42\u201343). Source: `workbenches/splitzero-tandem/continuations/20260914-recursive-source-relations/tex/incoming_source_metric_control.tex`, blob `b23bfcba6ec2dfcf35340a7d27c6f0a3145e83ea`.\n\nFinal head **`b4060b25c21f1a49a5e7730e9aff76d4c93c820d`** preserves that main snapshot and corrected PR #30 head **`aa6473075928b0316c49d50c163697c4ab98d004`**, with both ancestries. Against the inspected main there are **44 added files and no inherited modification/deletion**: 29 preserved PR30 files plus **15 new files in this continuation**. PR30 is still unmerged, so its additions appear in this main-based diff. Main, PR30's branch, publication files, and other-session refs are untouched. This PR is a draft, not a merge.\n\n## Observed successful verification\n\n**Implementation `04ef2f962d69186ef48f07679a339b57486ef471` passed [run 34797644407](https://github.com/KokunoYumeto/zeta-function-research-reader/actions/runs/34797644407).** Both [verify 103833747257](https://github.com/KokunoYumeto/zeta-function-research-reader/actions/runs/34797644407/job/103833747257) and [finite 103833747401](https://github.com/KokunoYumeto/zeta-function-research-reader/actions/runs/34797644407/job/103833747401) concluded successfully; both complete decoded logs were read. Verify finished at approximately **2026-09-14 02:04:04 UTC**. The final head adds only this workbench's README and STATUS, as separately confirmed by the commit comparison. It changes none of the verified sources, runner, tests, audit configuration, workflow, or dependencies. No later unobserved run is claimed green.\n\nAll **five new Lean modules** and their complete selected local closure\u2014**33 distinct local sources**\u2014passed individual `--trust=0 -DwarningAsError=true` checks. **60 selected new transitive axiom reports** passed with only subsets of `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`. The joint import includes the original boundary-socle maps, synchronization, conormal tower, and tau homotopy. Counts include definitions and interface lemmas, not discoveries. This is not a claimed rerun of the separate historical 60-target arithmetic-metric or 73-target derived Lean audits.\n\nUnchanged pins: Lean **4.31.0**, Mathlib **`fabf563a7c95a166b8d7b6efca11c8b4dc9d911f`**, original scalar blob **`ff991f7383922e71cdf0e4a3bc85e89e18f808ef`**. The workflow is read-only, with pinned checkout/toolchain dependencies.\n\n## The five completed modules\n\n**`SplitZeroResolventSeries`** constructs the finite polynomial `S_L=(I+H+...+H^L)T` and proves `X-S_L=H^(L+1)X` from `(I-H)X=T`. It proves the affine positive-spectrum bounds, centered variance identity, geometric residual bound, convergence for fixed data, and existence of a finite stopping degree. The constant term and exponent L+1 are retained.\n\n**`SplitZeroSignedTraceEnclosure`** proves the weighted Hilbert\u2013Schmidt trace inequality in the original positive source form. It constructs an isometry with both inverse laws from positive definiteness, proves conjugation and product-trace identities, applies Cauchy\u2013Schwarz, and returns to the original coordinates. The desired inequality is not assumed as a certificate field. For traceless original-metric-self-adjoint Q it proves the two-sided signed interval centered at `Re Tr(YQ)`, with error `sqrt(Re Tr(center(X-Y)^2) Re Tr(Q^2))`.\n\n**`SplitZeroCanonicalSignedResolvent`** derives Q from the four existing canonical residual sections and their actual inverse quotient Grams, allowing different relation dimensions. It proves Q is traceless and self-adjoint for the one common source form, ties its pairing to the four original quotient-Gram tangents, and inserts the constructed finite resolvent into the signed interval. No commutation of Q with the resolvent is assumed. Every mixed projector cross term remains.\n\n**`SplitZeroSpectralResidual`** transports the actual centered matrix residual to its complete spectral variance through explicit simultaneous-diagonalization equations for an isometry of the original metric. It proves `Tr(E_L^2)=sum delta_i^2-(sum delta_i)^2/n` and composes it with the trace estimate to obtain `|Re Tr(XQ)-Re Tr(S_L Q)| <= theta^(L+1) sqrt(K Re Tr(Q^2))`. The diagonalizing equations are required inputs, not an independently substituted diagonal matrix or a claimed verified general eigenvalue solver.\n\n**`SplitZeroRestrictedBoundary`** assembles the original coefficient quotient-kernel equivalence into natural SplitZero diagrams. For f:D\u2192E and original relation diagrams B,C with f(B)\u2286C, it constructs `(f^(-1)C)/B \u2243 ker(D/B\u2192E/C)`, both natural inverse maps, both inverse total-map laws, and the original quotient square. The exact image is characterized by `qf(y)=e*qf(y)`, not `qf(y)=tau`. A full-source boundary not admitted in the proper source remains a nonzero proper quotient class. Noninjective transports are allowed, and a present empty inner face under a nonbottom outer label remains distinct from external absence.\n\n## Exact finite checks and negative controls\n\nInherited source-resolvent **9 methods**, inherited mixed-metric **8 methods**, new signed-source **10 methods**, inherited boundary **9 ordered cases**, and **24 inherited checker unittests** passed normally and under `python -O`; successful JSON records matched. The new checker uses non-diagonal complex forms, actual polynomial relation columns/canonical sections for declared repeated-root fixtures, full cross terms, source-mass scaling, and proper-source quotient examples. These are not actual zeta packets or arithmetic moment integrals.\n\nFive false formulas\u2014`wrong-power`, `uncentered`, `diagonal-only`, `unweighted`, `proper-zero`\u2014were rejected in each mode. The gate checks exactly all five named records with `false_claim_accepted: false`; generic crashes do not count. Two separate Lean controls were rejected at their intended mathematical goals: the proposed `e=tau` proof, and a zero-degree finite sum falsely identified with its infinite geometric value.\n\nThe previous conversation summary and old PR30 body incorrectly said 11/15 recovered finite methods. **The correct observed counts are 9/8**, as already recorded at corrected PR30 head aa647307; that correction is preserved here. The new ten-method suite was also independently replayed locally in both modes with the same checker hash. Lean execution was remote GitHub Actions, not local.\n\n## Precise remaining scope\n\nThe fixed-pair finite error and stopping theorem are complete. They do not supply a uniform-in-tensor-degree arithmetic upper bound. The source's sharper nested-projector estimate **`8q-6`**, certified arithmetic moments, and the full path-integral certificate remain separate formalization/analytic inputs. The original full theta primitive and its Koszul signs do not automatically make it a primitive in every proper admitted source. Spectral nilpotents are not identified with inertia, and no general tensor-derived or six-functor theorem is claimed.\n\nFive failed development candidates and their exact proof/API or documentation-syntax repairs are retained in DEVELOPMENT and FINAL_DEVELOPMENT. No strict gate was disabled.\n\n**Full proof and source connection:** `workbenches/tau-signed-resolvent-formal/RESEARCH_NOTE.md`.\n**Observed execution, hashes, reproduction:** `STATUS.md`.\n**Next spectral/integration/proper-source interface:** `HANDOFF.md`.\n**Failures and repairs:** `DEVELOPMENT.md`, `FINAL_DEVELOPMENT.md`.",
